Meta-optimization criterion: all meta runs judge by the mean of the final organisms (distance of that mean to optimum). Lamarckian: mean of endpoints in last gen; Darwinian: mean of all organism points in last gen (full population, not just survivors). See summarize_final_state in core.py.

Measuring calculations (topology/fitness evaluations):
- Use CountedFunction from meta_evolution_functions: wrap your topology (e.g. rastrigin_func) and pass the wrapper to pure_darwinian_function / pure_lamarckian_function (or run_*_with_levers). After the run, read wrapper.n_calls.
- Darwinian: 1 evaluation per organism per generation → total = num_generations * population_size (per seed).
- Lamarckian: gradient uses 4 evaluations per child (finite differences) → total = num_generations * num_offspring * 4 (per seed). 